  paradroid/
      Paradroid (C64) by Andrew Braybrook, Hewson Consultants, 1985:
      the decks, blocks, characters, waypoints, lifts, droid types and
      pictures, the status panel, the ship's side view, the logo, the
      briefing, the console pages, the colours, the sound effects and
      the title's sound in data/ and in the build are taken from the
      original.

  simple-soccer/
      The graphics follow Arlasoft Soccer (C64). The title music player
      is the mixer of International Karate on the Plus/4 ("Wave Convert
      V2.0" by TLC of CNS, 1992). The title music is an arrangement of
      Kernkraft 400 (Zombie Nation, 1999) and Star Dust by David
      Whittaker (Lazy Jones, C64, 1984); the compositions belong to
      their owners. Sensible Soccer is by Sensible Software.

  demonattack/
      After Demon Attack (Atari 2600) by Imagic, 1982.

  phoenix/
      After Phoenix (Atari 2600, Atari, 1982; arcade game by Amstar /
      Centuri / Taito, 1980); the shapes are traced from the original,
      the melodies are the arcade game's.

  pacman/
      Pac-Man is a trademark of Bandai Namco Entertainment.

  stardew/
      Modelled on Stardew Valley by Eric Barone (ConcernedApe); nothing
      is taken from it. The music by Erik Satie is in the public domain.

  trainschedule/
      Modelled on Rail Route by bitrich. The compositions played (Johann
      Strauss I, Rossini, Offenbach, Lumbye, N.S. Smith, Tetsudo Shoka and
      others) are in the public domain; the notes of the Rossini overture
      come from an orchestral MIDI file at classicalmidi.co.uk.

